  "name": "LACTOSE TOLERANCE TEST",
  "code": "1134",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table class=\"border-borderMain my-[1em] w-full table-auto border\">\n<thead class=\"bg-offset\">\n<tr>\n<th class=\"border-borderMain px-sm py-sm dark:border-borderMainDark break-normal border text-left align-top\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">ime Point/Result</span></th>\n<th class=\"border-borderMain px-sm py-sm dark:border-borderMainDark break-normal border text-left align-top\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Interpretation</span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">&uarr;Glucose &gt; 30 mg/dL over baseline</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Normal: No lactose intolerance</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">&uarr;Glucose &lt; 20 mg/dL over baseline</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Suggests lactose intolerance</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">20&ndash;30 mg/dL increase</span></td>\n<td class=\"border-borderMain px-sm dark:border-borderMainDark min-w-[48px] break-normal border\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Borderline: Clinical correlation</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Normal:</strong>&nbsp;A rise in blood glucose &gt;30 mg/dL over fasting value at any point indicates adequate lactase activity and effective digestion of lactose.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Abnormal:</strong>&nbsp;A rise in blood glucose &lt;20 mg/dL suggests lactose intolerance due to insufficient lactase enzyme.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Symptoms:</strong> If patient develops GI symptoms (bloating, cramps, diarrhea) during or after the test, supports clinical diagnosis of lactose intolerance.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
